n present, emit one line naming `total` and the `by_step` counts; emit nothing when absent.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a test (or extend AC6) proving that a simulated failing call at the runner seam, under an activated gate scope, produces a non-empty drain that lands in coverage.llm_step_failures.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e","T6","T9"],"criteria":["E6","E1"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'A review-plan run in which one or more LLM step calls fail but the run still produces a verdict carries coverage.llm_step_failures'","AC6 enumerates: 'record→drain round-trip', 'no-failure run omits the key', 'record outside a scope is a no-op', 'drain is destructive', 'the verdict-assembly site adds the key only when non-empty' — none exercise the runner seam recording into an active gate scope"],"finding":"AC1 asserts an end-to-end outcome ('a review-plan run in which one or more LLM step calls fail ... carries coverage.llm_step_